#            supersession below happened before any B result existed, which is what makes it legitimate
#            rather than post-hoc fitting.
#
# history (each line: the checksum that was replaced, and why)
#   2026-09-21 09:20  15e71a0e5aa01cb31f5ffbb5267742795352dc6d218d52fd0bb48e961c58ee4e
#       First draft. Superseded the same day, before any result, by the common-capital revision:
#       - initial capital moved from an assumed 10000 USD to the common A/B/C/D value 7428.92 USD
#         (app.dev.bootstrap_paper_account.PAPER_INITIAL_CASH), with the A-baseline conflict recorded
#         rather than hidden: A's own backtest baseline still runs at 10000 (ASSUMED_RESEARCH), so USD
#         comparisons with A stay invalid until A is re-run. The capital-invariance derivation was
#         added to show the verdict metric survives the change.
#       - the derived 1R = 50 USD and 2000 USD position cap were deleted; they were parroting the old
#         capital. Sizing is declared as ratios of current realised equity, which is what the engine
#         actually does (Portfolio.enter passes self.equity), with the first-trade dollar values marked
#         as display only.
#       - costs restated as all-in per side (BASE 25, STRESS_30 30, STRESS_50 50; round trip is twice
#         each) with commission held at 10 and only the execution cost moving, because the commission
#         is a published schedule and the spread is the unmeasured quantity. The earlier levels were
#         stated as slippage alone, which left the round-trip figure ambiguous.
#       - the NEXT_BAR_OPEN fill rule and its signal-TTL deadline were written out, with the seven edge
#         cases registered for test. No fill becomes EXPIRED / SIGNAL_TTL, never an account refusal,
#         which is what the code already does; no enum, state or rule was added.
#       - the lift gate was made fully deterministic before results: cohorts by exact state and drop
#         reason, exclusion list, anchor and endpoint price definitions, the sparse-tape "last actual
#         close at or before the deadline" rule reused from F0 9.1, two separately counted missing-data
#         outcomes, the estimator, and the three lift outcomes with their thresholds.
#       - the verdict became a ranked, exhaustive decision order over PASS / BORDERLINE / FAIL /
#         INSUFFICIENT_SAMPLE / DATASET_NOT_READY / ERROR, so BORDERLINE cannot be defined after the
#         fact. The statistics block pins the reused C-E0 tool, block length 1, replicates, seed and the
#         percentile method.
#       - the universe became an immutable artifact with its own sha256 and no hardcoded count. The
#         3883-versus-3855 question was resolved as symbols versus contiguous missing-session runs
#         (3883 - 29 fully covered + 1 SPCX split = 3855, cross-checked by 29 x 104 + 21 = 3037), CON
#         was corrected from "absent from the universe" to "planned but skipped at fetch", and the
#         PIT statement was corrected: the union is a forward-looking superset and safety comes from
#         the per-session S(D) re-filter, which the readiness gate now checks.
#       - a STRICT dataset readiness gate, the forbidden flag list, run identity, artifacts and the
#         scope boundary against changing Strategy A or any strategy logic were added.
#   2026-09-21 10:05  66c3faceda6e50d4af527a010c5e9a499806ae64fe7d9c66becf878f9becd54f
#       The NEXT_BAR_OPEN deadline was wrong and the runner's tests caught it before any result.
#       The draft said the next actual bar could open as late as S + 3 minutes. Deriving it from
#       the code instead: the engine first asks the account at S + 2, fsm._entry_signalled expires
#       at elapsed >= signal_ttl_minutes, and a bar is available one minute after it opens, so the
#       latest reachable bar opens at S + signal_ttl_minutes - 1. At the declared TTL of 2 that is
#       S + 1 and nothing else: under NEXT_BAR_OPEN a single quiet minute after the signal bar
#       loses the trade outright. The contract now carries the formula, its derivation, the test
#       that pins it, and the consequence, which is the largest single risk to reaching the
#       30-trade sample gate on a sparse universe.
#   2026-09-21 12:40  73c4dd95038148a1b517b20e16e76ab557de397e92de76850e374f61a8ae7bfc
#       signal_ttl_minutes was not yet a committed term of this contract: the draft described the
#       fill deadline it observed but never declared the TTL, its units, its anchor or its boundary.
#       The new draft commits signal_ttl_minutes = 2 as RESEARCH_DEFAULT_PRECOMMITTED, in wall-clock
#       minutes, anchored at ENTRY_SIGNALLED, with an inclusive expiry
#       (next_actual_bar.open_time <= signal_at + signal_ttl_minutes), actual observed bars only,
#       same session only, synthetic bars never fillable. The value needed no code edit: the F0
#       config has carried 2 since its declaration and signal_ttl_bars exists nowhere.
#       Recording the declared window also made a disagreement explicit rather than leaving it
#       implied. The declared window admits a next actual bar at S+1, S+2 or S+3; the engine
#       reaches only S+1, because it asks the account one tick after the signal and the FSM expires
#       at elapsed >= ttl, leaving a single attempting tick. That also under-delivers against
#       B-F0 8.3's own sentence that the TTL gives the engine two ticks. The gap is carried as
#       implementation_gap.status = OPEN_BEFORE_FREEZE with both resolutions named, and the edge
#       case table now reports declared against measured per case. No strategy logic was changed.
#   2026-09-21 14:20  3747eeeb0dff131d3f9d0351a2be74502be64de30346bc7dd3228cafad4b53a7
#       Signal TTL contract semantics unchanged. The implementation gap was resolved and the
#       contract's evidence and status updated to match. This is NOT a threshold change: no
#       scanner gate, score weight, setup parameter, risk ratio, cost number, capital figure,
#       lift definition or entry session moved, and signal_ttl_minutes is still 2.
#       fsm._entry_signalled now expires on elapsed > signal_ttl_minutes + AVAILABILITY_DELAY
#       instead of elapsed >= signal_ttl_minutes, because a bar opening exactly on the declared
#       inclusive boundary is observable only one minute after it opens, so the last minute of
#       the declared window could never fill. The edge-case table now agrees on every row.
#   2026-09-21 15:10  9492c8120ad1a0a64dc61d8c1ebccfcf810c45219f1dc805275c8ad177eab56b
#       Documentation clarification only. The f0_prose_note said B-F0 8.3's "two ticks" sentence was
#       left for the user to amend; it has since been corrected in the F0 document, so the note now
#       records that correction instead of predicting it. No strategy threshold, no canonical rule,
#       no contract term and no code changed. The F0 rules JSON was not touched and its canonical
#       checksum a082b998... and file checksum were verified unchanged.
#   2026-09-21 18:30  7208926e91ad7f10181621def6881d3d36fe8cd8b5262cb3bf2746ef11421f16
#       The data adapter decisions D1 to D6 were approved and recorded, before any B result: scope
#       from the universe artifact only, grouped daily as B-E0's daily authority, IPO_WARMUP from
#       the first grouped-daily appearance, delisting and ticker-change filters NOT_APPLIED, minute
#       gaps excluded as pairs, and warmup gaps excluded from the RVOL baseline. The readiness gate
#       was pre-registered with its four statuses, the POLICY versus DATA_QUALITY split (only the
#       latter is counted), limits of 0.5% overall and 2% per session, and strictly-greater-blocks.
#       The readiness check "split records present for every symbol" was corrected: the dump covers
